<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alonso de Ojeda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1466–<a href="/years/1515">1515</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Alonso de Hojeda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alonso de Ojeda was a Spanish explorer who sailed on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a>'s second voyage in 1493. On <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a> he captured the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacique">cacique</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caonabo">Caonabo</a> by a ruse in 1495. He later led voyages along the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, naming Venezuela in 1499, and tried to found a colony at San Sebastián de Urabá in 1510, before dying poor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alonso-de-ojeda.jpg" alt="Alonso de Ojeda" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ignacio Castillo Cervantes · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conquistador_Alonso_de_Ojeda.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1495 <b>Alonso de Ojeda</b> captured him by a ruse, and he died at sea on the way to Spain.</blockquote><a href="/state/cacicazgo-of-maguana">Cacicazgo of Maguana</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Torrejoncillo del Rey, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/dominican-republic">the Dominican Republic</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=40.01,-2.57&amp;year=1497" aria-label="Torrejoncillo del Rey on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4487 732 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Alonso de Ojeda"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4937 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4937 1002h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=40.01,-2.57&amp;year=1497">What was here in 1497? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
